          "start": 711,
          "end": 712
        },
        {
          "text": "D.P. Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 720,
          "end": 728
        },
        {
          "text": "Anamika Kisku",
          "label": "JUDGE",
          "start": 759,
          "end": 772
        },
        {
          "text": "Ranchi",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 814,
          "end": 820
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "It appears that there was demand of dowry and to enforce the demand, she was tortured and ultimately she was driven away from the matrimonial home.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 866,
      "end": 1013,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "The matter was referred to the JHALSA for mediating the dispute between the parties.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1014,
      "end": 1099,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "JHALSA",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 1046,
          "end": 1052
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "Mediation report is available on the record, which shows that parties have settled the dispute.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1100,
      "end": 1195,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "Regard being had to the facts and circumstance of the case, I am inclined to enlarge the petitioner on anticipatory bail.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1196,
      "end": 1318,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "He is directed to surrender before the court below within two weeks from the date of receipt of copy of this order, and learned court below on his surrender shall release him on bail on furnishing bail bonds of Rs. 25,000/- (Twenty five Thousand only) with two sureties of the like amount each to the satisfaction of Smt. Anamika Kisku, learned Judicial Magistrate, 1 st Class,\nRanchi or her successor in connection with Namkum P.S. Case No.125/2020.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1319,
      "end": 1769,
